1
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:07,880
I don't want to be cute or someone who needs
protecting. I want to be a man you can rely on.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,080
It's all my fault.

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:12,000
Let me take care of you.

4
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:14,320
But I'm completely useless.

5
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,400
I really wanted to help.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,120
Then how about taking a
computer certification test?

7
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:20,559
It'll boost your confidence.

8
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,580
I'll take it.

9
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:26,020
You know,

10
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:30,680
I really like Okumi-san.

11
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:33,820
That should be fine.

12
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:35,700
That's awesome!

13
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:38,780
We're getting an intern
at the company soon.

14
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:40,359
An intern?

15
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:43,659
You're going to be a mentor. Do your best!

16
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:44,660
Got it.

17
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:46,600
It's been a while.

18
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:47,910
Hideaki.

19
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:01,700
Huh?

20
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,280
What happened?

21
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:11,040
Water just sprayed everywhere.

22
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:14,440
Anyway, put on one
of my shirts for now.

23
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:16,740
Sorry about this.

24
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:32,620
"Are the Sexy Buttocks Not Good?"

25
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:34,400
(Episode 6)

26
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:35,660
Just my luck.

27
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:41,000
Excuse me, where is the
General Affairs Department?

28
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:44,960
Sorry.

29
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:46,260
You're changing.

30
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,340
Who are you?

31
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:54,340
Anyway, you should probably
put some clothes on first.

32
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,840
May I ask who you are?

33
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:13,740
I'm a junior at Kaiyo University.
Kujo Hiroto.

34
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:15,040
Nice to meet you.

35
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,200
Nice to meet you too.

36
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:20,000
So this is the intern
that's been talked about.

37
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:25,400
I need to work hard too.

38
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:39,259
That's Hizaki, right?

39
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:41,320
- Yeah.
- How old is he?

40
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:46,500
I think he's turning 23 this year.

41
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:51,000
Ai-chan. Let's go.

42
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:56,700
Ah!

43
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:59,376
You'd better not get too close to him.

44
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:02,080
I don't really care about gender.

45
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:05,979
But Hizaki might.

46
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:07,460
Oh yes, maybe so.

47
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,499
He might already be seeing someone.

48
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:11,499
Wait, he's seeing someone?

49
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:16,080
Ah, oh, uhh, erm, I
don't really know for sure.

50
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:19,980
So that means he might be single.

51
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:25,060
No good.
He's way too optimistic.

52
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,400
I look forward to working
with you starting today.

53
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:29,700
Likewise.

54
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:33,440
There's still a lot I don't know.
I hope to learn a lot from you.

55
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:36,080
If you don't mind.

56
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:37,180
Oh.

57
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,880
I'm actually acting like a proper mentor.

58
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:41,360
However...

59
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,500
Please check this over.

60
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,239
- You're already done?
- Yes.

61
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,140
You learn fast.

62
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,190
Do you need any help?

63
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:53,760
What!?

64
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,100
I'm already done.

65
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:05,980
(I really hate myself for
trying to act like a mentor.)

66
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:09,540
Hizaki-san.

67
00:04:10,780 --> 00:04:13,450
('No one knows how to do it at first.')

68
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:16,850
(That's just empty talk to
someone who's actually capable.)

69
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:20,840
Hey, Kujo.

70
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:23,759
Why did you decide to
intern at our company?

71
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:25,460
Because I think it's a good company.

72
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:28,400
Plus, I have a relative working here.

73
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,640
- A relative?
- Yes.

74
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,480
I want to become someone like him.

75
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,960
I've looked up to him since I was a kid.

76
00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:38,560
What a good kid.

77
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:44,780
Being stared at like that
makes my heart race.

78
00:04:46,380 --> 00:04:47,560
Oh?

79
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:54,360
(I feel like this guy's reactions
are a lot like Okumi-san's.)

80
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:01,870
I heard the intern is
really attached to you?

81
00:05:02,770 --> 00:05:04,920
Rather than attached,

82
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:07,060
it's more like we hit it off right away.

83
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:10,840
Once he officially joins,
he'll probably surpass me in no time.

84
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:14,480
You'll grow during that time too.

85
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:16,520
I hope so.

86
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:19,060
(There it is again.
The elder's perspective.)

87
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:25,020
(When will I ever be able to
make Okumi-san rely on me?)

88
00:05:27,613 --> 00:05:31,700
Being stared at like that
makes my heart race.

89
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,280
Kujo is a bit like you, Okumi-san.

90
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:40,939
Well... actually,

91
00:05:41,615 --> 00:05:42,755
He's my nephew.

92
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,000
My older sister's kid.

93
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:45,600
Oh.

94
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:48,249
Wait, why didn't you tell me?

95
00:05:48,250 --> 00:05:52,509
You didn't tell me when you borrowed
someone else's shirt either.

96
00:05:52,510 --> 00:05:54,540
I wasn't trying to hide
it from you on purpose.

97
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:57,049
Do I look like the kind
of guy who would cheat?

98
00:05:57,050 --> 00:05:59,930
- Not at all.
- Then have a little more confidence.

99
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:02,700
You're right.

100
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:06,180
No, this is my own issue.

101
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:11,440
The time I spend with you
has a different meaning.

102
00:06:12,380 --> 00:06:14,699
After all, I'm nearly fourty and divorced.

103
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:16,720
And you've only just become an adult.

104
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:21,500
So for your future,
rather than being with someone like me,

105
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:24,020
there's definitely someone better...

106
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,879
Ai-chan?

107
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:33,480
What's wrong? What is it?

108
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:35,820
What are you doing?

109
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:37,100
Ai-chan.

110
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:39,159
It's my turn today.

111
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:44,160
Eh?

112
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:49,419
Are my feelings

113
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:51,699
really that untrustworthy?

114
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,860
That's not what I meant.

115
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:59,520
Just be a good boy and accept my love.

116
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:12,580
I've never taken the lead before.
Don't be disappointed if I'm bad at it.

117
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,560
Not at all.

118
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:18,579
Wait, is this your first time?

119
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:20,300
Shut up. Yes.

120
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,500
First time in my life.

121
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:27,000
Why are you already hard?

122
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:31,640
The body is pretty honest, huh?

123
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,240
You're such a hopeless old man.

124
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:12,300
I can't even remember
the last time we took a walk.

125
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:13,920
You need to exercise properly.

126
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:18,320
You're right. I need to keep my stamina up.
I don't want you to hate me.

127
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:20,240
I would never hate you.

128
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:23,120
Besides, you were
pretty energetic last night.

129
00:08:24,020 --> 00:08:25,420
So cute.

130
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:29,380
You really don't hold back
when it comes to this stuff, do you?

131
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:33,060
You have to speak your mind.

132
00:08:33,920 --> 00:08:37,200
Just thinking 'I really like you' in
my head won't reach your heart.

133
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:40,200
You're really holding nothing back.

134
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,780
Because I made a mistake once before.

135
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:45,600
So I decided,

136
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,920
I will absolutely never
make the same mistake twice.

137
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:55,560
After all, neither my time nor yours
is infinite.

138
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:06,080
(Have I ever seriously told him
that I like him?)

139
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:14,120
(Can I just suddenly say,
'I like you too'?)

140
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:17,080
What's wrong?

141
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:22,180
(But I think I kind of get it now.)

142
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:25,000
After all, I'm the
second-generation successor.

143
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,956
Back then, I couldn't even worry
about whether I was gay or bisexual.

144
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:31,160
The time I spend with you
has a different meaning.

145
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:36,220
(Even though I still have a lot of
immature things to worry about,)

146
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:40,400
(Okumi-san has his own
insecurities and worries too.)

147
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:45,080
Sorry, hold on a second.

148
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:52,299
I also feel... for Okumi-san...

149
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:54,060
- Mom!
- Coming!

150
00:09:55,190 --> 00:09:56,990
- Kids.
- Kids?

151
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:59,080
You're the president.
What about a successor?

152
00:09:59,290 --> 00:10:02,160
- It's impossible if you're with me.
- I can't give birth either.

153
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,920
But I can stay by your side, Ai-chan.

154
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:13,720
And I can make you feel good
as many times as you want.

155
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:16,000
Horny old man.

156
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:20,500
Hey, what's wrong with that?

157
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:38,240
Hizaki-san and Hideaki?

158
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:52,400
(Even though it's sudden,)

159
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:56,940
(It's the company's busy season right now.)

160
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:04,660
I'm back.

161
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:13,879
It's really busy this time of year.

162
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:14,880
Yeah.

163
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:18,020
That being said, it's my first year too,
so it's my first time experiencing it.

164
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:20,340
(So he's his nephew.)

165
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:25,640
(Their vibes and everything
really are a bit similar, huh.)

166
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:32,780
Is there something on my face?

167
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:34,680
Nothing.

168
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:37,260
Just wondering what you're eating.

169
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:40,159
This? It looked
good, so I bought it.

170
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:41,580
Want a bite?

171
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:43,299
Can I?

172
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:45,460
- Go ahead, go ahead.
- Awesome.

173
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:49,960
Just a bite.

174
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,839
Say ah.

175
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:52,840
Ah.

176
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:08,300
Sorry about that.

177
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:10,420
I have a much younger brother,

178
00:12:10,740 --> 00:12:12,180
so I just did it without thinking...

179
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,560
I brought the documents.

180
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:18,979
What's wrong?

181
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:19,980
Are you really that busy?

182
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:24,220
Do you have any stomach medicine?

183
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:27,600
- Huh?
- Ah...

184
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,179
Good work today.

185
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:42,930
- Good work.
- Hizaki-san, are you seeing anyone?

186
00:12:43,830 --> 00:12:45,080
Huh?

187
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:47,800
(Next Episode Preview)
That person is super cute, right?

188
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,060
I'm going to get seriously mad.

189
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:52,320
I'm really glad you came,

190
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:55,620
but if you're busy, wouldn't it be
better to talk after you get home?

191
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:58,460
If it were me,
I would never make Hizaki-san cry.
